========================================================================================
MEASURED lag-1 Spearman autocorrelation of ||dX_t||
   Spearman, not Pearson: it is invariant to the marginal, so it is
   comparable across two series with different tail indices -- which a
   Pearson autocorrelation at these tails would not be.
========================================================================================
   Treasury curve           lean/replication/data/fred_cache.npz     panel   (2494, 11)   n =  2494   rho_S = +0.3034
   commercial-paper curve   data/cp_nasdaq.npz                       panel    (4396, 6)   n =  4396   rho_S = +0.5906

========================================================================================
INVERTING THE DESIGN -- which phi reproduces each measured rho_S?
   The copula-AR(1) design drives a Gaussian AR(1) with parameter phi
   through Phi and then the inverse Pareto CDF.  Both maps are monotone,
   so Spearman is preserved EXACTLY and phi maps to rho_S through the
   Gaussian-copula relation rho_S = (6/pi) arcsin(phi/2), not phi = rho_S.
   That distinction was never checked when phi = 0.3 / 0.6 were fixed.
========================================================================================
