   series                       rho_S   phi used   phi implied   kappa impact
   Treasury curve             +0.3034       0.30         0.320             ok
   commercial-paper curve     +0.5906       0.60         0.608             ok

   READING.  If phi_implied differs materially from the phi that was
   used, kappa was calibrated at the wrong persistence and every
   theta-hat downstream inherits it.  kappa is DECREASING in phi (more
   persistence -> a larger max-to-sum ratio at the same n), so a phi that
   is too small makes kappa too LARGE, which makes the selector too
   PERMISSIVE -- it would accept a smaller theta than it should.

